<h2>Country comparison</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Gulf states</strong> — high vehicle ownership, import-led replacement, telecom and data-centre backup; heat is the dominant design constraint.</li>
<li><strong>North Africa</strong> — local assembly in some markets, solar and telecom demand, and a growing two-wheeler segment.</li>
<li><strong>Sub-Saharan Africa</strong> — solar home systems, telecom backup and replacement batteries; logistics and service access decide the total cost.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What to verify</h2>
<p>Ask for the derated life at the actual ambient temperature, the warranty route and the spare-part supply. In markets where service is difficult, a slightly more expensive product with local support is often the lower-cost choice.</p>
