<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Why do batteries fail faster in hot climates?</h3>
<p>Heat accelerates grid corrosion and water loss in lead-acid, and accelerates calendar aging in lithium. A product rated for 25 °C may lose a large part of its life at 40 °C; specify a derated life or a more heat-tolerant design.</p>
<h3>Is local assembly common in the region?</h3>
<p>In some markets, yes — usually for lead-acid SLI or pack assembly from imported cells. Check the country page and the manufacturer directory before assuming a local supplier is a local manufacturer.</p>
